    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d425">

                <pb facs="0610" n="486" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg486"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.48B/198: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Woods</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-10-13T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 13,
                                1923—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>219. Following for you.</p>
                <p>“October 13, Number 23. Have purchased all commodities listed your 76<anchor
                        n="33" xml:id="d425-f1"/> costing about two and half million dollars. Advise
                    Japanese Bureau we have additional $3,000,000 now available for expenditure.
                    Large quantities food, clothing and shelter supplies available, here. If wanted
                    cable specific requisition. Payne Amcross.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
